s4-4-p43 : Block
s4-4-p43 = prose (cons "The last equality follows inductively by cancellation of the two child factorials. The information \(\log_2(n!)\) is thus independent of the tree, while (4.28) depends on it. Binary comparisons have a worst-case lower bound \(\lceil\log_2(n!)\rceil\); balanced merging at \(n=2^k\) uses at most \(nk-n+1\). At \(n=8\), these are \(16\) and \(17\), respectively. Adjacent swaps measure a different quantity: the inversion count, lowered by exactly one when an adjacent out-of-order pair is corrected. The comparison identifies order; the swap changes an enumeration." nil)
